      "headline": "Kyoto is the cultural heart of Japan, serving as the nation's imperial capital for over a millennium and remaining a repository of traditional arts, architecture, and history.",
      "body": [
        "Located in the Kansai region of Honshu, Kyoto acted as the seat of the Japanese Emperor from 794 until 1868. This long tenure as the capital fostered a refined aesthetic culture that permeates the city, from its meticulous Zen gardens and wooden tea houses to the intricate rituals of the geisha districts.",
        "Today, the city bridges the gap between historical preservation and modern urban life, housing a population of approximately 1.43 million. It remains globally significant for its dense concentration of cultural treasures, including 15 UNESCO World Heritage Sites that protect its irreplaceable shrines, temples, and historic districts."
      ],
      "caveats": [
        "The 2025 census figure is the most recent official data provided."
      ]
    },
